# Loop head merges a conditional element write

Verifies a write that only one iteration performs still reaches the next
iteration. The first iteration stores `2cm`; the second reads that stored
centimeter value, so the output is `11mm` and then `21mm`.

>>> source
let a: int[] = [10mm]

for (i in 0..2) {
    print(a[0] + 1mm)
    if (i == 0) {
        a[0] = 2cm
    }
}

<<< stdout
11mm
21mm

<<< stderr
